# The `finally` Block

The `finally` block is a control structure used in exception handling that **always executes**, regardless of whether an exception was thrown or caught. It is commonly used for cleanup operations that must run no matter what.

## Syntax (Java, C#, Python, JavaScript, etc.)

```java
try {
    // Code that might throw an exception
} catch (ExceptionType e) {
    // Handle the exception
} finally {
    // This code ALWAYS runs
}
```

## Key Characteristics

| Scenario | Does `finally` run? |
|---|---|
| No exception thrown | ✅ Yes |
| Exception caught | ✅ Yes |
| Exception not caught (propagates) | ✅ Yes |
| `return` in `try`/`catch` | ✅ Yes (before returning) |
| `break`/`continue` in `try` | ✅ Yes |
